EXT. PETTING ZOO - BIRTHDAY PARTY - DAY

A fenced paddock, hay bales, a goat in a party hat. Kids shriek in the distance.

DARIUS FENWICK-ODOM (40s, host dad, apron over a polo) carries a tray of juice boxes to the pen, whistling. His wife SOLEDAD (40s, sunglasses, a phone in each hand) trails him, texting. Her mother PAULINE (70s, lawn chair, thermos) watches from the gate. The ZOO KEEPER, MR. RIBEIRO (50s, overalls, bucket), leans on a fence post.

He sets down the tray. She sets down a phone. Pauline lifts her thermos in salute.

DARIUS
Seven kids. One goat. What could go wrong?

MR. RIBEIRO
Don't say that.

SOLEDAD
(not looking up)
Darius, don't.

PAULINE
(over her)
Let the man speak.

The goat lowers its head. It eyes the tray. It eyes Darius.

DARIUS
Nice goat.

MR. RIBEIRO
That's Gerald.

SOLEDAD
Gerald is wearing a party hat.

PAULINE
So is the cake.

They all turn. Behind them, the cake sits on a hay bale, fully intact, a three-tier unicorn. Gerald trots toward it.

DARIUS
Gerald, no.

MR. RIBEIRO
Gerald, heel!

SOLEDAD
Mother, move your chair!

Gerald hits the hay bale at a full run. Frosting rains over all four of them. Pauline, sprayed pink from head to toe, lowers her thermos and says, perfectly calm:

PAULINE
Well. That's a fun party.
